  "canonical_name": "K-Means Algorithm",
  "definition": {
    "status": "grounded",
    "grounding_mode": "contextual_synthesis",
    "text": "The K-means algorithm is a clustering approach equivalent to a statistical mixture model and, for Euclidean data, a special case of the EM algorithm; it assumes clusters are spherical Gaussian distributions with different means and equal covariance matrices.",
